@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@samp{sgn} is a full-featured Signal messenger client for Emacs, designed to replace Signal Desktop for daily use.  It communicates with a running @samp{signal-cli} daemon via JSON-RPC and persists all message history locally in an SQLite database with full-text search. @*

The user experience is modeled after @samp{telega}, the Telegram client for Emacs.  Chat buffers use a header-plus-body grouping style, with text properties on every message enabling point-based commands for reactions, replies, editing, deletion, and more.  A dashboard buffer provides a chat list with unread badges, last-message previews, and pinned chats. @*

The package is split into focused modules: @*

@itemize
@item
@samp{sgn.el} --- Entry point, autoloads, and top-level commands. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-rpc.el} --- JSON-RPC subprocess management, send/receive, retry logic. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-db.el} --- SQLite persistence layer with FTS5 full-text search. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-chat.el} --- Chat buffer mode with telega-style rendering and input handling. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-actions.el} --- Message actions: react, reply, edit, delete, forward, pin. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-contacts.el} --- Contact/group cache and completing-read interface. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-media.el} --- Inline images, stickers, voice notes, link previews. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-format.el} --- Text formatting: render Signal styles, compose markup. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-notify.el} --- Modeline/tab-bar unread indicator and desktop notifications. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-search.el} --- FTS5-powered search across conversations. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-dashboard.el} --- Chat list buffer with sorting, unread tracking, and fade-out truncation. @*
@item
@samp{sgn-import.el} --- One-time import of history from Signal Desktop. @*
@end itemize

@strong{Prerequisites}: @*

@enumerate
@item
Emacs 29.1 or later, compiled with SQLite and FTS5 support. @*
@item
@samp{signal-cli} v0.14+ installed and in @code{$PATH}, with a registered or linked Signal account. @*
@item
Optional: ImageMagick (@samp{convert}) for animated sticker conversion; @samp{sox} for voice note recording; @samp{sqlcipher} CLI for Signal Desktop import. @*
@end enumerate

The package has no external Emacs package dependencies --- it uses only built-in libraries. @*

The development repository is on @uref{https://github.com/benthamite/sgn, GitHub}. @*

