@node Account and program paths
@section Account and program paths

@vindex sgn-account
@vindex sgn-cli-program
@vindex sgn-data-directory
@vindex sgn-db-directory
The user option @code{sgn-account} specifies the registered Signal phone number, for example @samp{+15550000000}.  This must match the account registered with @samp{signal-cli}.  The value is required: @code{sgn-start} will signal an error if it is @code{nil}.  The default is @code{nil}. @*

The user option @code{sgn-cli-program} specifies the path to the @samp{signal-cli} executable.  If @samp{signal-cli} is on your @code{$PATH}, the default value (the result of @code{executable-find}) should work without modification. @*

The user option @code{sgn-data-directory} specifies the directory where @samp{signal-cli} stores its data, including attachments and sticker packs.  The default is @samp{~/.local/share/signal-cli}.  You would change this if you installed @samp{signal-cli} with a non-standard data path. @*

The user option @code{sgn-db-directory} specifies the directory where @samp{sgn} stores its SQLite database.  The default is @samp{~/.local/share/sgn}.  The directory is created automatically on first run. @*

@node Message display
@section Message display

@vindex sgn-history-page-size
@vindex sgn-message-grouping-interval
@vindex sgn-timestamp-format
@vindex sgn-prompt
The user option @code{sgn-history-page-size} controls how many messages are loaded into a chat buffer when it is first opened.  The default is 50.  Increase this if you want to see more history immediately; decrease it for faster buffer creation. @*

The user option @code{sgn-message-grouping-interval} specifies the number of seconds within which consecutive messages from the same sender are grouped under a single header.  The default is 300 (five minutes).  Set this to 0 to disable grouping entirely, or increase it to group messages over longer spans. @*

The user option @code{sgn-timestamp-format} controls how message timestamps are displayed.  It accepts three values: @code{smart} (the default) shows relative time for recent messages and absolute time for older ones; @code{absolute} always shows the full date and time; @code{relative} always shows relative time (e.g., ``5m'', ``2h''). @*

The user option @code{sgn-prompt} specifies the input prompt string displayed at the bottom of chat buffers.  The default is @samp{"> "}. @*

@node Media rendering
@section Media rendering

@vindex sgn-image-max-width
@vindex sgn-sticker-max-width
@vindex sgn-enable-animation
The user option @code{sgn-image-max-width} sets the maximum pixel width for inline image rendering in chat buffers.  The default is 300.  Increase this on high-resolution displays or if you want larger image previews. @*

The user option @code{sgn-sticker-max-width} sets the maximum pixel width for sticker images.  The default is 150.  Stickers are typically smaller than photos, so a separate limit keeps them from appearing disproportionately large. @*

The user option @code{sgn-enable-animation} controls whether stickers and GIFs are animated.  The default is @code{t}.  Set this to @code{nil} if animations are distracting or cause performance issues. @*

@node Messaging behavior
@section Messaging behavior

@vindex sgn-auto-open-buffer
@vindex sgn-send-read-receipts
@vindex sgn-cli-auto-read-receipts
@vindex sgn-send-typing
The user option @code{sgn-auto-open-buffer} controls whether a chat buffer is automatically displayed when an incoming message arrives.  The default is @code{nil}, meaning new messages only update the unread count and trigger notifications.  Set this to @code{t} if you want Emacs to switch to the relevant chat buffer on each incoming message. @*

The user option @code{sgn-send-read-receipts} controls whether @samp{sgn} sends read receipts via @code{sendReceipt} when a chat buffer is visible and focused.  The default is @code{t}.  This is @emph{focus-gated}: receipts are only sent when you are actually looking at the chat, preserving your privacy when you have a chat buffer open but unfocused. @*

The user option @code{sgn-cli-auto-read-receipts} controls whether the @samp{--send-read-receipts} flag is passed to @samp{signal-cli} at the process level.  The default is @code{nil}.  When enabled, @samp{signal-cli} sends read receipts for @emph{every} incoming data message regardless of Emacs focus.  Most users should leave this off and rely on @code{sgn-send-read-receipts} instead. @*

The user option @code{sgn-send-typing} controls whether typing indicators are sent to your chat partner while you compose a message.  The default is @code{t}. @*

@node Notifications
@section Notifications

@vindex sgn-notification-style
@vindex sgn-desktop-notifications
The user option @code{sgn-notification-style} determines where the global unread count indicator is displayed.  It accepts two values: @code{modeline} (the default) adds a @samp{[sgn:N]} indicator to the global mode line; @code{tab-bar} adds a segment to the tab bar instead.  The indicator is managed by the minor mode @code{sgn-global-mode} (@ref{Global indicator}). @*

The user option @code{sgn-desktop-notifications} controls whether desktop notifications are shown for incoming messages.  The default is @code{t}.  Notifications are suppressed for muted chats.  On macOS, notifications use AppleScript; on Linux, they use D-Bus via @code{notifications-notify}. @*

