@node Starting and stopping
@section Starting and stopping

@findex sgn-start
@findex sgn-stop
@findex sgn-show-log
The command @code{sgn-start} initializes the @samp{sgn} Signal client.  It validates that SQLite and @samp{signal-cli} are available, initializes the database, loads the contact cache, starts the JSON-RPC subprocess, subscribes to incoming messages, refreshes contacts, and enables the global unread indicator.  Call this once at the beginning of your session. @*

The command @code{sgn-stop} shuts down the client.  It stops the JSON-RPC subprocess, cancels all timers (contact refresh, message expiration), closes the database, and disables the global indicator. @*

The command @code{sgn-show-log} displays the @samp{*sgn-log*} debug buffer.  This buffer records all JSON-RPC traffic and internal events, which is useful for troubleshooting connectivity or message delivery issues. @*

@node Opening chats
@section Opening chats

@findex sgn-chat
@findex sgn-note-to-self
@findex sgn-dashboard
The command @code{sgn-chat} prompts for a recipient using @code{completing-read} over all contacts and groups, sorted by recency.  Each candidate carries a hidden stable chat ID, so selection works correctly even when multiple contacts share a display name.  Annotations show unread counts and relative timestamps. @*

The command @code{sgn-note-to-self} opens the ``Note to Self'' chat, which is the conversation with your own Signal account. @*

The command @code{sgn-dashboard} opens the chat list buffer (@ref{Dashboard}). @*

@node Sending messages and media
@section Sending messages and media

@findex sgn-chat-send-input
@findex sgn-attach-file
@findex sgn-send-voice-note
The command @code{sgn-chat-send-input} sends the text in the input area to the current chat.  If a reply is in progress, the message is sent as a quoted reply; if an edit is in progress, the message replaces the original.  Lightweight markup in the input (@samp{*bold*}, @samp{_italic_}, @samp{~strikethrough~}, @samp{`monospace`}, @samp{||spoiler||}) is parsed into Signal style ranges before sending.  Bound to @code{RET} in chat buffers. @*

The command @code{sgn-attach-file} sends a file as an attachment to the current chat.  It prompts for a file path interactively.  Bound to @code{C-c C-a}. @*

The command @code{sgn-send-voice-note} is a placeholder for recording and sending voice notes.  It is not yet implemented. @*

@node Message actions
@section Message actions

These commands operate on the message at point in a chat buffer.  Point can be anywhere within a message's text property region. @*

@findex sgn-react
@findex sgn-reply
@findex sgn-edit
@findex sgn-delete
@findex sgn-forward
@findex sgn-copy-text
@findex sgn-toggle-pin
@findex sgn-chat-cancel-action
The command @code{sgn-react} sends a reaction to the message at point.  It prompts with @code{completing-read} over common emoji (by name, e.g., ``thumbs up'', ``heart'').  You can also type an emoji character directly.  If you have already reacted to the message, invoking @code{sgn-react} again removes your reaction.  Bound to @code{r}. @*

The command @code{sgn-reply} sets up a quoted reply to the message at point.  The input prompt changes to show the quoted context.  Press @code{C-g} (@code{sgn-chat-cancel-action}) to cancel.  Bound to @code{q}. @*

The command @code{sgn-edit} places the text of your own message at point into the input area for editing.  Only your own messages can be edited.  The edited text is sent with @code{editTimestamp} so Signal replaces the original.  Press @code{C-g} to cancel.  Bound to @code{e}. @*

The command @code{sgn-delete} performs a remote delete of your own message at point.  It prompts for confirmation with @code{y-or-n-p}.  The message is marked as deleted both locally and for all recipients.  Bound to @code{d}. @*

The command @code{sgn-forward} sends the text of the message at point to another chat selected via @code{completing-read}.  Bound to @code{f}. @*

The command @code{sgn-copy-text} copies the message text at point to the kill ring.  Bound to @code{c}. @*

The command @code{sgn-toggle-pin} pins or unpins the message at point.  If the message is already pinned, it is unpinned; otherwise, it is pinned.  Pinned messages display a pin indicator in the chat buffer.  Bound to @code{P}. @*

The command @code{sgn-chat-cancel-action} cancels an in-progress reply or edit, clearing the input area and restoring the normal prompt.  If no action is in progress, it falls through to @code{keyboard-quit}.  Bound to @code{C-g}. @*

@node Polls
@section Polls

@findex sgn-create-poll
@findex sgn-vote-poll
The command @code{sgn-create-poll} creates a new poll in the current chat.  It prompts for a question and then repeatedly prompts for options until you enter an empty string.  At least two options are required. @*

The command @code{sgn-vote-poll} votes in the poll at point.  It displays the available options via @code{completing-read} and sends the vote to the group. @*

@node Searching
@section Searching

@findex sgn-search
@findex sgn-search-in-chat
@findex sgn-search-refresh
@findex sgn-search-goto-result
@findex sgn-search-next-result
@findex sgn-search-prev-result
The command @code{sgn-search} performs a full-text search across all conversations using FTS5.  It prompts for a query string and displays results in a @samp{*sgn Search*} buffer.  Each result shows the sender, timestamp, a snippet with highlighted matches, and a link to the source chat.  Deleted messages are excluded. @*

The command @code{sgn-search-in-chat} restricts the search to the current chat buffer. @*

The command @code{sgn-search-refresh} re-runs the most recent search query. @*

In the search results buffer, @code{sgn-search-goto-result} (bound to @code{RET}) opens the chat containing the result at point.  @code{sgn-search-next-result} (@code{n}) and @code{sgn-search-prev-result} (@code{p}) navigate between results. @*

@node Dashboard
@section Dashboard

@findex sgn-dashboard
@findex sgn-dashboard-refresh
@findex sgn-dashboard-open
@findex sgn-dashboard-mark-read
@findex sgn-dashboard-toggle-mute
@findex sgn-dashboard-toggle-pin
The dashboard is a @code{tabulated-list-mode} buffer named @samp{*sgn*} that displays all conversations sorted by last message timestamp, with pinned chats always at the top.  Each row shows the chat name, a last-message preview, a relative timestamp, and an unread count.  Chats with unread messages are displayed in bold.  Long text is truncated with a fade-out gradient effect instead of an ellipsis. @*

The command @code{sgn-dashboard-open} opens the chat at point.  Bound to @code{RET}. @*

The command @code{sgn-dashboard-mark-read} marks the chat at point as read and resets its unread count.  Bound to @code{d}. @*

The command @code{sgn-dashboard-toggle-mute} mutes or unmutes the chat at point.  Muted chats suppress desktop notifications.  Bound to @code{M}. @*

The command @code{sgn-dashboard-toggle-pin} pins or unpins the chat at point.  Pinned chats are sorted to the top of the list.  Bound to @code{P}. @*

The command @code{sgn-dashboard-refresh} reloads the dashboard data from the database.  Bound to @code{g}.  The dashboard also refreshes automatically when new messages arrive. @*

@node Group and contact management
@section Group and contact management

@findex sgn-create-group
@findex sgn-set-disappearing
@findex sgn-block-contact
@findex sgn-unblock-contact
@findex sgn-contacts-refresh
The command @code{sgn-create-group} creates a new Signal group.  It prompts for a group name and then repeatedly prompts for member phone numbers until you enter an empty string. @*

The command @code{sgn-set-disappearing} sets the disappearing message timer for the current chat.  It prompts for a duration in seconds; entering 0 disables the timer.  The command dispatches to @code{updateGroup} for groups and @code{updateContact} for individual chats. @*

The command @code{sgn-block-contact} blocks a contact after confirmation.  The command @code{sgn-unblock-contact} unblocks a previously blocked contact.  Both prompt for the contact via @code{completing-read}. @*

The command @code{sgn-contacts-refresh} fetches the latest contacts and groups from @samp{signal-cli} and updates both the in-memory cache and the database.  This runs automatically on startup and periodically, but you can invoke it manually if a contact name has not yet updated. @*

@node Global indicator
@section Global indicator

@findex sgn-global-mode
The minor mode @code{sgn-global-mode} activates the global unread count indicator.  When enabled, it displays the total unread message count in either the mode line or tab bar, depending on the value of @code{sgn-notification-style} (@ref{Notifications}).  This mode is enabled automatically by @code{sgn-start} and disabled by @code{sgn-stop}. @*

@node Text formatting
@section Text formatting

@findex sgn-format-reveal-spoiler-at-point
The command @code{sgn-format-reveal-spoiler-at-point} reveals spoiler text at point.  Spoiler messages arrive with foreground and background colors matched so the text is concealed; this command swaps the face to @code{sgn-spoiler-revealed-face} to make the text readable. @*

@node Importing from Signal Desktop
@section Importing from Signal Desktop

@findex sgn-import-from-desktop
The command @code{sgn-import-from-desktop} performs a one-time import of message history from Signal Desktop's SQLCipher database into @samp{sgn}'s SQLite database.  This requires the @samp{sqlcipher} CLI tool (installable via @samp{brew install sqlcipher} on macOS) and a local Signal Desktop installation. @*

The import process exports Signal Desktop's encrypted database to a temporary plain SQLite file, builds conversation and identity mappings, imports all messages with their metadata (quotes, expiration timers, raw JSON), and then imports reactions.  The temporary file is deleted after the import completes. @*

On macOS, the command automatically handles both the legacy plain-text key and the newer Chromium safeStorage encrypted key format, decrypting via the macOS Keychain and Node.js. @*

@node Miscellaneous
@section Miscellaneous

@findex sgn-open-at-point
@findex sgn-load-more-history
The command @code{sgn-open-at-point} opens media or follows a link at point.  If point is on a button (such as an attachment or link preview), it activates it.  Bound to @code{RET} in the message area. @*

The command @code{sgn-load-more-history} loads older messages from the database.  Pagination by timestamp cursor is not yet implemented.  Bound to @code{g} in chat buffers. @*

