@node Contact resolution
@section Contact resolution

@findex sgn-contacts-get-name
@findex sgn-contacts-set-name
@findex sgn-contacts-display-sender
@findex sgn-contacts-completing-read
@findex sgn-contacts-load-from-db
The function @code{sgn-contacts-get-name} returns the display name for a Signal ID (phone number or group ID).  If no name is cached, it returns the ID itself as a fallback. @*

The function @code{sgn-contacts-set-name} stores a display name for a Signal ID in the in-memory cache.  This is called automatically when messages arrive with sender name information. @*

The function @code{sgn-contacts-display-sender} returns a display string for a sender.  If SENDER matches @code{sgn-account}, it returns @samp{"You"}; otherwise it resolves the name via @code{sgn-contacts-get-name}. @*

The function @code{sgn-contacts-completing-read} presents a @code{completing-read} interface for selecting a chat.  Candidates are sorted by recency and annotated with unread counts and relative timestamps.  Duplicate display names are disambiguated with a phone number or group ID suffix.  Returns the selected chat ID, not the display name. @*

The function @code{sgn-contacts-load-from-db} loads contact names from the database into the in-memory cache.  Called during startup. @*

@node Chat buffer management
@section Chat buffer management

@findex sgn-chat-get-buffer
@findex sgn-chat-open
@findex sgn-chat-insert-message
@findex sgn-chat-update-message
@findex sgn-chat-show-typing
@findex sgn-chat-clear-typing
@findex sgn-chat-insert-system-msg
@findex sgn-chat-message-at-point
The function @code{sgn-chat-get-buffer} returns the buffer for a given chat ID, creating it if necessary.  Buffer names follow the pattern @samp{*sgn: <display-name>*}.  When a name collision occurs (two different chats with the same display name), a disambiguating suffix is appended. @*

The function @code{sgn-chat-open} opens a chat buffer and switches to it, positioning point at the end and marking the chat as read. @*

The function @code{sgn-chat-insert-message} renders a new incoming or sync message into the appropriate chat buffer.  It inserts before the input prompt and scrolls to the bottom if the buffer is visible. @*

The function @code{sgn-chat-update-message} re-renders a specific message by its ROWID@.  This is used after edits, deletions, or reaction changes to refresh the display. @*

The function @code{sgn-chat-show-typing} displays a typing indicator for a given sender in the header line of the appropriate chat buffer.  The indicator auto-clears after ten seconds. @*

The function @code{sgn-chat-clear-typing} removes the typing indicator from the current buffer's header line. @*

The function @code{sgn-chat-insert-system-msg} inserts a system message (such as an error or status notification) into a chat buffer.  The message is rendered with a configurable face, defaulting to @code{sgn-error-face}. @*

The function @code{sgn-chat-message-at-point} returns a plist describing the message at point, including @code{:rowid}, @code{:timestamp}, @code{:sender}, @code{:chat-id}, and @code{:target-author}.  This is the foundation for all point-based message actions (@ref{Message actions}). @*

@node Database operations
@section Database operations

@findex sgn-db-init
@findex sgn-db-close
@findex sgn-db-search
@findex sgn-db-purge-expired
The function @code{sgn-db-init} initializes the SQLite database.  It creates the database directory if needed, verifies FTS5 support, enables WAL journaling, and creates all tables on first run.  Called by @code{sgn-start}. @*

The function @code{sgn-db-close} closes the database connection. @*

The function @code{sgn-db-search} performs a full-text search using FTS5.  It accepts a QUERY string, an optional CHAT-ID to restrict the search, and an optional LIMIT@.  Results include a @code{:snippet} key with highlighted matches delimited by brackets.  Deleted messages are excluded. @*

The function @code{sgn-db-purge-expired} deletes messages whose expiration timestamp has passed.  It runs periodically on a timer started by @code{sgn-start}. @*

@node RPC layer
@section RPC layer

@findex sgn-rpc-start
@findex sgn-rpc-stop
@findex sgn-rpc-alive-p
@findex sgn-rpc-send
@findex sgn-rpc-send-message
The function @code{sgn-rpc-start} starts the @samp{signal-cli} JSON-RPC subprocess.  It resets all internal state and launches the process with a filter and sentinel for handling incoming data. @*

The function @code{sgn-rpc-stop} stops the subprocess. @*

The function @code{sgn-rpc-alive-p} returns non-nil if the subprocess is running. @*

The function @code{sgn-rpc-send} sends a generic JSON-RPC request.  It accepts a METHOD name, PARAMS alist, and optional CALLBACK function.  The callback is invoked with the result when a successful response arrives.  Transient errors on idempotent methods (send, sendReaction, sendReceipt, sendTyping) are automatically retried once after a short delay. @*

The function @code{sgn-rpc-send-message} is a convenience wrapper that sends a text message to a chat ID, with optional extras (attachments, quote parameters, edit timestamp). @*

@node Media rendering (1)
@section Media rendering

@findex sgn-media-insert
@findex sgn-media-insert-inline-image
@findex sgn-media-find-sticker
@findex sgn-media-insert-voice-note
@findex sgn-media-play-audio
@findex sgn-media-insert-link-preview
The function @code{sgn-media-insert} is the main entry point for rendering media in a chat buffer.  It handles both attachments (images, files) and stickers, dispatching to the appropriate rendering function. @*

The function @code{sgn-media-insert-inline-image} creates and inserts an Emacs image object from a file path.  It respects @code{sgn-image-max-width} and animates multi-frame images when @code{sgn-enable-animation} is non-nil. @*

The function @code{sgn-media-find-sticker} locates the local file for a sticker by pack ID and sticker ID@.  It first checks the pack's @samp{manifest.json}, then falls back to searching by numeric ID with common extensions. @*

The function @code{sgn-media-insert-voice-note} inserts a clickable voice note element displaying the duration and a play button. @*

The function @code{sgn-media-play-audio} plays an audio file.  It prefers Emacs's built-in @code{play-sound-file} when available, falling back to external players (@samp{afplay} on macOS, @samp{paplay} or @samp{aplay} on Linux). @*

The function @code{sgn-media-insert-link-preview} renders a box-drawing framed link preview with title, description, domain, and optional thumbnail.  Pressing @code{RET} on the preview opens the URL in a browser. @*

@node Text formatting (1)
@section Text formatting

@findex sgn-format-apply-styles
@findex sgn-format-parse-markup
@findex sgn-format-styles-to-json
The function @code{sgn-format-apply-styles} applies Signal text style ranges to a string.  It accepts TEXT and a STYLES-JSON string (a JSON array of objects with @code{start}, @code{length}, and @code{style} keys).  The supported styles are BOLD, ITALIC, STRIKETHROUGH, MONOSPACE, and SPOILER, each mapped to an appropriate Emacs face.  Spoiler text additionally receives the @code{sgn-spoiler} text property for use by @code{sgn-format-reveal-spoiler-at-point} (@ref{Text formatting, , Text formatting commands}). @*

The function @code{sgn-format-parse-markup} parses lightweight markup in user input.  It returns a plist with @code{:text} (the plain text with delimiters removed) and @code{:styles} (a list of style alists ready for Signal's API).  The supported markup delimiters are @samp{*bold*}, @samp{_italic_}, @samp{~strikethrough~}, @samp{`monospace`}, and @samp{||spoiler||}.  Backslash-escaped delimiters are treated as literals. @*

The function @code{sgn-format-styles-to-json} serializes a list of style alists into a JSON array string suitable for database storage. @*

@node Notification helpers
@section Notification helpers

@findex sgn-notify-update
@findex sgn-notify-message
The function @code{sgn-notify-update} recalculates the global unread count from the database and updates the modeline or tab-bar indicator.  Muted chats are excluded from the count. @*

The function @code{sgn-notify-message} shows a desktop notification for a new message.  It is suppressed for muted chats.  The notification includes the sender name and a truncated message preview. @*

@node Mention and poll rendering
@section Mention and poll rendering

@findex sgn-actions-apply-mentions
@findex sgn-actions-render-poll
The function @code{sgn-actions-apply-mentions} applies mention highlighting to a text string.  Mentions of self use @code{sgn-mention-self-face}; mentions of others use @code{sgn-mention-face}. @*

The function @code{sgn-actions-render-poll} renders a poll into the current buffer, displaying the question, options with vote bar charts, vote counts, and a voting prompt (or ``Poll closed'' indicator). @*

